WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.830
The paper makes three contributions.

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:07.740
First, it proposes DARTFormer,

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.650
a differentiable-architecture-search-style method
that efficiently finds the best attention for a task.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.560
Second,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.470
it extends that framework to build and search for
heterogeneous Transformers that combine multiple attention types,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.380
using two procedures: an expensive iterative
pruning method they call NAS Prune,

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.290
and a cheap single-pass method called NAS One-shot.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.200
Third, and most importantly,

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.110
it shows empirically that these heterogeneous
Transformers cannot outperform the best

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.020
homogeneous Transformer on the long-range NLP tasks
studied.
